{
  "requirement": "An explicit access key consists of its ID and secret. Supply `session_token` when using temporary credentials.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct BedrockCredentials {\n    pub access_key_id: SecretString,\n    pub secret_access_key: SecretString,\n    pub session_token: Option<SecretString>,\n}\n\nimpl BedrockCredentials {\n    pub fn new(access_key_id: SecretString, secret_access_key: SecretString) -> Self;\n    pub fn session_token(self, session_token: SecretString) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for BedrockCredentials;\nimpl Debug for BedrockCredentials;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for BedrockCredentials;\nimpl PartialEq for BedrockCredentials;\nimpl Serialize for BedrockCredentials;\nimpl Eq for BedrockCredentials;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement states the struct shape, two constructors/builders, and six trait implementations.\n\n- **`new`**: `backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs` calls `BedrockCredentials::new(\"id\", \"secret\")`. It asserts the serialized form is exactly `{access_key_id:\"id\", secret_access_key:\"secret\"}`. That shows the two fields hold the right values and `session_token` is `None` and absent.\n- **`session_token` builder**: the same test builds `permanent.clone().session_token(\"token\")`. It asserts the result differs from `permanent`. It then asserts the nested Bedrock config serializes with `session_token: \"token\"` alongside the other two fields.\n- **Serialize and Deserialize**: the same test round-trips the permanent form, with no token, through `from_value` and `to_value`. `all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials` round-trips a Bedrock config whose credentials include `session_token`. It asserts exact JSON equality and equality after a string round trip.\n- **Clone**: `permanent.clone()` is exercised.\n- **PartialEq**: both `assert_eq` and `assert_ne` are used.\n- **Debug**: `assert_eq!` on `BedrockCredentials` values needs Debug, so it is compiled in.\n- **Eq**: it is a marker trait with no behavior of its own.\n- **Struct shape and exports**: `public_exports_match_the_appendix` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs` checks the public API inventory against rustdoc and compiles the Habeas consumer against the SDK.\n\nI found no obligation without a test, and no plausible violation of the text that these tests would accept.",
